and we are joined once again on the  programme by the vaccines minister  nadeem sahabi mrs howie really good to  see you this morning um and it does feel  having dipped my toe into social media  this morning seen some concern seeing  plenty of misinformation it feels like  we all need to take a few deep breaths  this morning because we are talking  about vaccinating children can you just  repeat the justification that was given  to the public yesterday by the chief  medical officer why do we feel it is  necessary  for 12 to 15 year olds to receive a  vaccine  absolutely good morning uh neil so uh  the joint committee on vaccination  immunization who have relied upon and  have they have delivered throughout the  vaccine deployment program have been on  your show many times  beginning uh back last year when we  launched with the fisa bionic vaccine on  the 8th of december um the jcbi uh  looked at the clinical um uh impact on  12th year olds and  came down on the side that that actually  being vaccinated is marginally better  but not enough to  recommend a universal vaccination  program they recommended that the chief  medical officers of england wales  scotland northern ireland  look at  the other public health and mental  health impacts on children not on the  wider population on those 12 15 year  olds  they reported yesterday and they have  unanimously all four chief medical  officers england scotland wales and  northern ireland have recommended that  we offer a one uh dose of the fisa  biontech vaccine to 12 year olds now the  way we will do that is uh and we've  accepted that advice  is through the school school-age  immunization service which has been  doing  vaccination of children for many many  years very well-versed doing this so  clinicians will lead on this in school  schools  will contact parents in the usual way  that they do and will require consent  parental consent uh of course and this  is voluntary there is no stigmatization  of any parent or  anyone who may choose not to have the  vaccine although i have to say when we  offered the vaccine last month the 16  and 17 year olds they came forward um in  the past month in their droves and their  numbers because they realize that how  important it is to protect themselves  and of course they've seen firsthand the  damage that the covert pandemic has has  done to mental health and of course  through schools as well but but just  just to go back to the rationale for  this part of the concern as i understand  it from parents who've expressed concern  is that we have in essence you know  clinical advice being given for  non-clinical purposes we have we have  doctors  advising 12 to 15 year olds to follow a  medical process a vaccination  for reasons which don't seem to have a a  grounding in the clinical side and  that's worrying people  and that's really important to uh sort  of  try and flesh out for your viewers  the chief medical officers  were asked the jcbi the joint committee  actually recommended that we ask the  chief medical officers  we asked them they also consulted with  the royal colleges of pediatrics  the royal college of gps and of course  the jcbi were in the room uh to look at  the mental health  impact on those 12 13 year olds at the  public health impact on the 12 15 years  not on the greater uh uh sort of good of  society it's actually for those  12 to 15 year olds the jcbi  were only sort of looking at what they  are narrowly qualified to look at which  is why they made the recommendation that  we should also ask the chief medical  officers they have now come back to us  and they recommend uh  the offer of a single dose uh for 12  year olds with parental consent so that  is what we'll be going ahead and doing  it's been a very just honest incentive  sorry  we've really got a finite amount of time  this morning i'm really keen to kind of  get through as many questions as  possible on the consent point how will  that be how will that be administered  again of course and a bit of  disinformation on social media this  morning i mean isn't it the case that  you know 12 to 15 year olds can you know  right now consent to other forms of of  medical treatment where their parents  perhaps have a different view  so the consent process the  school age immunization service um  are really  really well equipped to do they've been  doing it for years  for children's vaccination in schools so  children will have a leaflet that they  can share with their parents and of  course we'll have a consent form  that will go to them either  electronically or in some schools  physically to their parents and the  parents will then read all the  information  have to give consent if the child is to  be vaccinated on the very rare  occasions where there is a difference  opinion of opinion between the parent  and the 12 to 15 year old  where the parent for example doesn't  want to give consent but the 12 to 15  year old wants to have the vaccine then  the first step is the clinician of the  school immunization  service will bring the parent and the 12  to 15 year old the child together to see  whether they can reach consent if that  is not possible then if the child is  deemed to be competent and this has been  around since the 80s for all  vaccination programs for example in  schools if the child is deemed to be  competent the gillig competence as it's  referred to  then the child can have the vaccine but  these are very rare um  occasions and it is very important to  remember that the school  age immunization service is incredibly  well equipped to deal with this  clinicians are very well versed in  delivering vaccinations to 12 year olds  in schools  sure  let's talk though about about the winter  plan and this was something we explored  with with your colleague therese coffee  yesterday it is absolutely fair to say  isn't it that despite that the clear  inclination to avoid lockdowns to avoid  reintroduction mandatory face masks  socia